{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Hark fair traveler of distant lands prepare thy soul for Japan’s wondrous realm where cherry blooms do dance and mountains stand as ancient sentinels of time.  \nThou shalt arrive in Kyoto where moss doth whisper secrets to the stones and temples bow in silent prayer beneath the moon’s soft gaze.  \nThere walk the paths of Arashiyama where bamboo sways as if in courtly dance and monkeys chuckle in the groves of yore.  \nThen haste thee to Nara where deer with eyes of wisdom bow before thee and shrines hum with the breath of gods long known.  \nFrom there thy feet shall carry thee to the fiery peaks of Fuji whose crown doth pierce the heavens and whose reflection in Lake Kawaguchi doth mirror heaven’s own face.  \nIn Tokyo the neon rivers flow like liquid stars and bustling streets doth sing the song of progress yet still the quiet tea houses breathe with grace.  \nThou shalt taste the sushi fresh as morning tide and savor sake that warms the heart like fire in winter’s chill.  \nIn Hakone the steam doth rise from hot springs where thou shalt bathe beneath the stars and dream of samurai and poets who walked this earth before thee.  \nAt last thou shalt journey to the island of Miyajima where the torii gate doth stand as if it walks upon the sea and the bells of Itsukushima ring with the voice of eternity.  \nReturn home with a heart full of silence and a soul alight with beauty for Japan doth not merely show thee sights but teacheth thee to see.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.09076494723558426}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0023813480511307716}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -1.7260669469833374}, {"token": " traveler", "logprob": -0.09184246510267258}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.890907883644104}, {"token": " distant", "logprob": -0.01264200545847416}, {"token": " lands", "logprob": -0.2958679497241974}, {"token": " prepare", "l